# Terms belonging to the tenants this repository is NOT. One extended regular expression per line;
# matched case-insensitively against every staged path and every staged byte. Whole-line comments
# and blank lines are ignored. A commit staging a match is refused.
#
# Write the OTHER tenants, never an allowlist of this one: nobody can enumerate in advance every
# term their own work will legitimately contain, and a control that refuses unfamiliar material is
# a control people bypass on the first false refusal.
#
# See protocol/doctrine/tenancy.md. An empty file polices nothing, which is the honest state until
# you have a second tenant.

# Each client, employer or organization this repository is not. Names, product names, domains.
# Example:  Initech
#           initech\.example

# Internal codes and planning references that have no business leaving their own repository.
# The two below exclude a preceding `.`, `/`, `-` or `_`, so a filename extension is not read as a
# code. Delete them if this tenant has no such convention.
# (^|[^A-Za-z0-9._/-])W[0-9]{2,3}([^0-9A-Za-z]|$)
# (^|[^A-Za-z0-9._/-])P[0-9][a-z]?([^0-9A-Za-z]|$)

# Identifier shapes that are always somebody's infrastructure. Uncomment the ones that apply.
# [0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}
# (^|[^0-9.])(10|192\.168)\.[0-9]{1,3}\.[0-9]{1,3}\.[0-9]{1,3}
# (^|[^0-9])[0-9]{12}([^0-9]|$)
